{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1489596918,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMTQ0NTY3NTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1371","origin":"github"},"title":"housekeeping helper command (probably just extend 'clean' with few more actions)","message":"I tend to do manually for now from time to time following errands manually for each (sub)dataset.  Primarily triggered by automated crawling, which can blow things up quite considerably ;)\n\n- dropping unused content, generally the one not pointed by a branch or a tag\n```\ngit annex unused --used-refspec +refs/heads/master:+refs/heads/incoming:+refs/tags/*\ngit annex dropunused all \n```\nso if may be would could specify some policy `datalad-cleanup-unused-refspec` so if specified, this step would be performed -- would be neat\n\n- git gc -- since we, to avoid side-effects from interaction of GitPython's in-memory view with our direct invocation of git commands, we disable gc while running git commands, we should run it manually from time to time.   So I just do\n\n```\ngit gc --prune=now \n```","files":null}]}